  written for one question: what a reversal does to the totals (03 §9).

  The IBANs, names and amounts belong to no one. Real bank data never enter the
  repository — they stay on the user's machine (03 §6.1).

  Eight entries, chosen so that every arm of 03 §9 has a row:

    1  -40.00  direct debit, an ordinary expense
    2  +2500.00  salary, an ordinary credit — income and nothing else
    3  +40.00  the reversal of 1, carrying RvslInd AND RtrInf (§9.4)
    4  -25.00  a second ordinary expense
    5  +25.00  the reversal of 4, carrying RtrInf only and no RvslInd (§9.4)
    6  -18.00  a card payment
    7  +18.00  a credit from the same shop with NO reversal evidence at all —
               a positive amount, an equal and opposite one, and an expense
               category are exactly what §9.5 says do not prove a reversal
    8  -12.00  a second card payment, so the categories below are not all zero

  Opening 1000.00, movements +2488.00, closing 3488.00.
-->
